 and NSYNC and the like.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 30 - The Sweet Sound of 70s Bubblegum Music","url":null}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Glamour in Pop Music Videos","body":"NSYNC's expensive music videos contributed to the return of glamour in pop music during the mid to late 1990s. Their visual style stood in contrast to the unpolished, authentic aesthetic favored by the alternative rock scene at the time. \"Glamour returned to pop music with expensive videos from Britney Spears, Backstreet Boys, and InSync.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The Rise and Fall and Future of the Music Video - Part 2","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7IDbqdIw3WU"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Produced by Max Martin","body":"Max Martin composed all the hits for *NSYNC, establishing his reputation as a major hitmaker for pop stars. \"había hecho todos los éxitos de 5 de los en sync de un montón de estrellas.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Music Radar Clan","episode":"Poniendo a Britney Spears en su lugar","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ad2agh7IXH8"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Rise of Pop Music","body":"NSync was among the pop artists that defined the musical tastes of Generation Y towards the end of the 1990s, reflecting a shift away from brooding grunge and post-punk alt-rock. \"This cheerful generation led us to an era of spice girls and backstreet boys in sync, Britney Spears.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The 90s Part 9: The Festivals","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7JP2tjJibTQ"}]}],"awards":[],"concerts":[],"xref":[{"kind":"xref","title":"1996 Pop Resurgence","body":"NSYNC (referred to as \"Sink\") was listed among the artists who contributed to the resurgence of pop music from 1996, marking a period where pop began to challenge and eventually dominate the music 